End":15},"content":"<p>as I. 10:34-44 the Holy Ghost. 10:45,46; 19:6 as on. 2:2-12; 4:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-16","title":"Acts 11:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>remembered. 20:35; Lu 24:8; Joh 14:26; 16:4; 2Pe 3:1 how. 1:5; 19:2-4; Mt 3:11; Mr 1:8; Lu 3:16; Joh 1:26,33 but. Pr 1:23; Isa 44:3-5; Eze 36:25; Joe 2:28; 3:18; 1Co 12:13; Tit 3:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-17","title":"Acts 11:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>as God. 15; 15:8,9; Mt 20:14,15; Ro 9:15,16,23,24; 11:34-36 what. 10:47; Job 9:12-14; 33:13; 40:2,8,9; Da 4:35; Ro 9:20-26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-18","title":"Acts 11:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>they held. Le 10:19,20; Jos 22:30 and glorified. 15:3; 21:20; Isa 60:21; 61:3; 2Co 3:18; Ga 1:24 hath. 1; 13:47,48; 14:27; 22:21,22; Ro 3:29,30; 9:30; 10:12,13; 15:9-16 Ga 3:26,27; Eph 2:11-18; 3:5-8 granted. 3:19,26; 5:31; 20:21; 26:17-20; Jer 31:18-20; Eze 36:26; Zec 12:10 Ro 10:12,13; 15:9,16; 2Co 7:10; 2Ti 2:25,26; Jas 1:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-19","title":"Acts 11:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>they. 8:1-4 Phenice. 15:3; 21:2 Cyprus. 4:36; 13:4; 15:39; 21:16 Antioch. 26; 15:22,35 to none. 3:26; 13:46; Mt 10:6; Joh 7:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-20","title":"Acts 11:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Cyrene. 2:10; 6:9; 13:1; Mt 27:32 the Grecians. 6:1; 9:29 preaching. 8:5,35; 9:20; 17:18; 1Co 1:23,24; 2:2; Eph 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-21","title":"Acts 11:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>the hand. 2Ch 30:12; Ezr 7:9; 8:18; Ne 2:8,18; Isa 53:1; 59:1; Lu 1:66 and a. 24; 2:47; 4:4; 5:14; 6:7; 1Co 3:6,7; 1Th 1:5 turned. 9:35; 15:19; 26:18-20; 1Th 1:9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-22","title":"Acts 11:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>A.M. 4047. A.D. 43. tidings. 1; 8:14; 15:2; 1Th 3:6 and they. 4:36,37; 9:27; 13:1-3; 15:22,35-39</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-23","title":"Acts 11:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>seen. Mr 2:5; Col 1:6; 1Th 1:3,4; 2Ti 1:4,5; 2Pe 1:4-9; 3Jo 1:4 and exhorted. 13:43; 14:22; Joh 8:31,32; 15:4; 1Th 3:2-5; Heb 10:19-26,32-39 2Pe 3:17,18; 1Jo 2:28 purpose. Ps 17:3; Pr 23:15,28; Da 1:8; 2Co 1:17; 2Ti 3:10 cleave. De 10:20; 30:20; Jos 22:5; 23:8; Mt 16:24; 1Co 15:58</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-24","title":"Acts 11:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>he was. 24:16; 2Sa 18:27; Ps 37:23; 112:5; Pr 12:2; 13:22; 14:14; Mt 12:35 Mt 19:17; Lu 23:50; Joh 7:12; Ro 5:7 full. 6:3,5,8; Ro 15:15 and much. 21; 5:14; 9:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-25","title":"Acts 11:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>to Tarsus. 9:11,27,30; 21:39</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-26","title":"Acts 11:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>that. 13:1,2 with the church. 14:23,27; 1Co 4:17; 11:18; 14:23 taught. Mt 28:19 were. 26:28; Isa 65:15; 1Co 12:12; Eph 3:15; 1Pe 4:14; 1Jo 2:27; Re 3:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-27","title":"Acts 11:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>prophets. 2:17; 13:1; 15:32; 21:4,9; Mt 23:34; 1Co 12:28; 14:32; Eph 4:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-28","title":"Acts 11:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>Agabus. 21:10 great.This was probably the famine which took place in the fourth year of Claudius, which continued for several years, and in which, says Josephus, \"many died for want of food.\"</p>\n<p>Ge 41:30,31,38; 1Ki 17:1-16; 2Ki 8:1,2 Claudius.Claudius Caesar succeeded C. Caligula, A.D. 41; and after a reign of upwards of 13 years, he was poisoned by his wife Agrippina, and succeeded by Nero.</p>\n<p>Lu 2:1; 3:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-29","title":"Acts 11:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>every. Ezr 2:69; Ne 5:8; 1Co 16:2; 2Co 8:2-4,12-14; 1Pe 4:9-11 to send. 2:44,45; 4:34; Ec 11:1,2; Lu 12:29-33; Ro 15:25-27; 1Co 13:5; 16:1 2Co 9:1,2; Ga 2:10; Heb 13:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-11-30","title":"Acts 11:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>to the. 14:23; 15:4,6,23; 16:4; 20:17; 1Ti 5:17; Tit 1:5; Jas 5:14; 1Pe 5:1 by. 12:25; 1Co 16:3,4; 2Co 8:17-21</p>"}]}